   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend part U1 of chapter 62 of the laws of 2003, amending the\nvehicle and traffic law and other laws relating to increasing certain motor\nvehicle transaction fees, in relation to the effectiveness thereof; to amend\npart B of chapter 84 of the laws of 2002, amending the state finance law\nrelating to the costs of the department of motor vehicles, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon\nexpiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S9631",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9631-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Part U1 §13, Chap 62 of 2003; amd Part B §2, Chap 84 of 2002",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9631\n\nSPONSOR: KRUEGER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend part U1 of chapter 62 of the laws of 2003, amending the\nvehicle and traffic law and other laws relating to increasing certain\nmotor vehicle transaction fees, in relation to the effectiveness there-\nof; to amend part B of chapter 84 of the laws of 2002, amending the\nstate finance law relating to the costs of the department of motor vehi-\ncles, in relation to the effectiveness thereof; and providing for the\nrepeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would extend various expiring laws that allow the Department\nof Motor vehicles to collect certain fees and pay operating costs.\n\n* Section 1 extends Section 1 of Part G of Chapter 58 of the Laws of\n2024, which authorizes the Department of Motor Vehicles to collect\nrevenue from certain fees relating to motor vehicle transactions and the\ndeposit of revenue collected from taxes imposed by Section 183 and 184\nof Tax Law.\n\n* Section 2 extends Section 2 of Part B of Chapter 84 of the Laws of\n2002, which allows revenue in the Dedicated Highway and Bridge Trust\nFund to be used for DMV expenses.\n\n \nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS:\n\nEnactment of this bill is necessary for the continuation of certain\nprograms, the collection of necessary revenues and the disbursement of\nfunds.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall be repealed upon enact-\nment of legislation constituting the 2026-27 budget.\n",
